# CRAN — `\value` docs and console I/O

These rules come from CRAN review feedback (glmbayesCore and the CRAN Cookbook). Follow them whenever editing `R/` or `man/` in this package so submissions do not regress.

## 1. Exported functions must document `\value`

- Every exported function / S3 method documented with roxygen **must** have `@return` that becomes `\value` in the Rd file.
- Describe **structure** (list components, class names, atomic type/length) and **meaning** of the return value.
- If called only for side effects: `@return No return value, called for side effects.` (or equivalent).
- Edit the **roxygen source** in `R/`, then re-run `devtools::document()` / `roxygen2::roxygenise()`. Do **not** only patch generated `man/*.Rd` files.
- Exception: `\docType{data}` datasets do not need `\value`.

Cookbook: https://contributor.r-project.org/cran-cookbook/docs_issues.html#missing-value-tags-in-.rd-files

## 2. No ungated `print()` / `cat()` for ordinary messages

CRAN expects console chatter to be suppressible and R-like.

**Do:**

- Use `message()` for informational notes users may suppress with `suppressMessages()`.
- Use `warning()` / `stop()` for problems.
- Gate progress or developer noise with `if (isTRUE(verbose)) message(...)` (or an existing `progbar` / quiet option).
- For diagnostic or summary **reports**, return an object (optionally with a class) and implement `print.<class>()`; let interactive auto-print show the report. Assigned results stay quiet until `print(x)`.

**Allowed exceptions:**

- S3 `print.*` / `print.summary.*` methods (and similar interactive printers).
- `packageStartupMessage()` on attach when appropriate.
- The `stats::glm`-style `print(family)` immediately before `stop("'family' not recognized")` is acceptable if matching base R.

**Do not:**

- Call `print("...")` or ungated `cat(...)` inside ordinary modelling / check / sampler functions to emit status text.
- Rely on `inst/WORDLIST` alone for DESCRIPTION spelling; package/API names in `Description` go in single quotes; use `.aspell/` (UTF-8 **without BOM**) for remaining technical terms if needed.

Cookbook: https://contributor.r-project.org/cran-cookbook/code_issues.html#using-printcat

## 3. Before finishing a docs or console-touching change

1. Confirm new/changed `@export` symbols have `@return`.
2. Grep `R/` for ungated `cat(` / `print(` outside S3 print methods.
3. Re-document if roxygen changed.
